{#
/**
 * @file
 * The song page (INT8-019) — FR-12, FR-14, FR-15, FR-17.
 *
 * REVIEW ROUND 2 (2026-07-26): this template originally replaced core's
 * node.html.twig outright, which silently dropped the <article> wrapper,
 * `attributes` (the node--type-song / node--view-mode-full classes,
 * contextual-links attributes) and the title_prefix/title_suffix hooks other
 * modules attach to — a real accessibility/SEO and module-compatibility
 * regression, caught in review rather than by a test (nothing in this
 * project's suite asserts the node's own wrapper element). Rebuilt to keep
 * that structure, mirroring core/starterkit's own node.html.twig, with only
 * the CONTENT arrangement inside customised.
 *
 * The page's one <h1> is supplied site-wide by INT8-028's page-header hero
 * block, not by this template — so unlike core's own node.html.twig (which
 * conditionally prints an <h2> title when `view_mode != 'full'`), no title
 * heading is printed here at all: this template is suffixed `--full`, so
 * that condition is always false for it anyway.
 *
 * FR-12's negative half (no type/group) and FR-14 (no releases, setlist,
 * tabs, studio) are satisfied by OMISSION: `field_song_type`,
 * `field_parent_song` and friends are hidden on the `full` view display
 * (core.entity_view_display.node.song.full.yml) and nothing below prints
 * them by name. There is no suppression logic to get wrong.
 *
 * Field ORDER is controlled here, not by the display's field weights: the
 * hi-fi's SONG PAGE composition puts the quote ABOVE the lyrics, which a
 * plain field-order render can't express without reordering every other
 * field's weight to match — the quote is the one field genuinely out of
 * document order relative to the rest.
 *
 * `content.field_x|render|trim` (not `node.field_x.isEmpty()`) is the
 * emptiness check throughout: it asks "would this actually render
 * something", which also respects field access — a field an anonymous
 * visitor cannot see is correctly treated as absent, not merely unset.
 *
 * The "coming soon" rail moved out of this template entirely (review round
 * 2) — it is now the `i8_song_sidebar` block, placed in the theme's new
 * `sidebar_second` region and composed into a real two-column layout by
 * page.html.twig, not hardcoded here. It held no field content and needed
 * no per-node data, so a block was strictly the right shape for it — this
 * template only ever needed to render the node's own fields.
 *
 * INT8-020 (FR-13, FR-20) — song versions. `alternate_of`, `same_as_parent`,
 * `parent_lyrics` and `alternate_versions` all come from
 * interstate_85_preprocess_node__song(): none of them is expressible as a
 * plain field render, since they either need a SECOND entity's field
 * (the parent's lyrics) or a reverse reference no field on this entity
 * carries (which other songs point back at it).
 *
 * When `alternate_of` is set, the plain single-column LYRICS section below
 * is replaced by the `lyric-pair` SDC (THIS VERSION | NORMAL VERSION) —
 * never both; a song is either a standard lyrics page or an alternate's
 * comparison view, matching FR-20's scope. The column labels inside it are
 * plain markup reusing `.section-label`'s own classes, not a nested
 * `{% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}`: embedding one SDC's embed
 * inside a block passed to ANOTHER embed (`lyric-pair`'s `this_version`/
 * `normal_version` blocks) is the same class of nesting that already broke
 * `views-view--songs.html.twig` and is avoided here for the same reason,
 * not assumed safe.
 *
 * Cross-links to the parent use the `link` component's `inline`/`action`
 * variants (design-system.md §3 — plain-colour inline links failed Axe's
 * `link-in-text-block`, WCAG 1.4.1: a link inside running text needs more
 * than colour to read as a link, which `link--inline`'s underline gives it).
 * Only the TWO links outside `lyric-pair` (the cross-reference line below,
 * and the alternate-versions list) are genuine `{% embed 'interstate_85:link' %}`
 * calls — safe, since neither sits inside another component's block. Doing
 * that at least once per page is also what attaches `link.css` at all: an
 * SDC's CSS is only attached where it is genuinely rendered, not wherever
 * its class names are reused, so the two links INSIDE `lyric-pair` above
 * (same reasoning as the labels — no nested embed) rely on one of these two
 * having already put `link.css` on the page. Both are on every page that
 * can reach them: an alternate's own page always has the cross-reference
 * link; a parent's page always has the alternates list.
 */
#}
{%
  set classes = [
    'node',
    'node--type-' ~ node.bundle|clean_class,
    node.isPromoted() ? 'node--promoted',
    node.isSticky() ? 'node--sticky',
    not node.isPublished() ? 'node--unpublished',
    'node--view-mode-' ~ view_mode|clean_class,
  ]
%}
{% set has_quote = content.field_quotes|render|trim %}
{% set has_lyrics = content.field_lyrics|render|trim %}
{% set has_notes = content.field_notes|render|trim %}
{% set has_video = content.field_video|render|trim %}

<article{{ attributes.addClass(classes) }}>
  {{ title_prefix }}
  {{ title_suffix }}

  <div{{ content_attributes.addClass('song-detail') }}>
    {% if has_quote %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:quote-block' %}
        {% block quote %}{{ content.field_quotes }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if alternate_of %}
      <p class="song-detail__alt-link">
        {{ 'Alternate title/lyrics for →'|t }}
        {% embed 'interstate_85:link' with {href: alternate_of.url, variant: 'inline'} %}
          {% block label %}{{ alternate_of.label }}{% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
      </p>

      {% embed 'interstate_85:lyric-pair' %}
        {% block this_version %}
          <div class="section-label section-label--default">{{ 'This version'|t }}</div>
          {% if same_as_parent %}
            <p class="song-detail__same-as-parent">
              <a class="link link--inline" href="{{ alternate_of.url }}">{{ '[same as normal version]'|t }}</a>
            </p>
          {% elseif has_lyrics %}
            <div class="song-detail__lyrics">{{ content.field_lyrics }}</div>
          {% endif %}
        {% endblock %}
        {% block normal_version %}
          <div class="section-label section-label--default">
            {{ 'Normal version'|t }} —
            <a class="link link--inline" href="{{ alternate_of.url }}">{{ alternate_of.label }}</a>
          </div>
          <div class="song-detail__lyrics">{{ parent_lyrics }}</div>
        {% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
    {% elseif has_lyrics %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Lyrics'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <div class="song-detail__lyrics">{{ content.field_lyrics }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if has_notes %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Notes'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <div class="song-detail__notes">{{ content.field_notes }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if has_video %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Video'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <div class="song-detail__video">{{ content.field_video }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if alternate_versions %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Alternate versions'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <ul class="song-detail__alternates">
        {% for alternate in alternate_versions %}
          <li>
            {% embed 'interstate_85:link' with {href: alternate.url} %}
              {% block label %}{{ alternate.label }}{% endblock %}
            {% endembed %}
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</article>
